# Accepted findings for tools/audit-public.py.
#
# One rule per line:   kind | path-glob | literal | reason
#
#   kind       finding kind (e.g. email, home-path, generic-secret) or "*"
#   path-glob  fnmatch glob against the repository path ("*" crosses "/")
#   literal    optional substring of the matched text; empty accepts any match
#   reason     required; why publishing this is fine
#
# Never put source-machine strings (username, hostname, company domain, device
# names), real emails or tokens here: those belong only in the private strings
# file kept outside the repository.
#
# Pseudo paths: <commit-metadata> <tag-metadata> <ref> <commit> .gitmodules
# The literal is matched against the matched text or its whole source line.

email | <commit-metadata> | Co-Authored-By: Claude | AI co-author trailer; vendor noreply address, identifies no person
generic-secret | tests/test-clipboard-helpers.sh | CLIPBOARD_CANARY_ | synthetic canary payload proving the clipboard helpers never log contents
